WEBVTT

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:11.520
In the unknown reaches of time, strange and wondrous creatures appeared on this planet.

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:14.150
We call them Pokémon.

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:17.880
Over the years, countless varieties of Pokémon developed.

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:24.930
Researchers have identified hundreds of different types, but many more are yet to be discovered.

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:30.000
Many tales have been passed down of the extraordinary adventures we humans shared with our Pokémon.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.960
friends. There have been conflicts too, but over the ages we learned to live

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:40.830
together in harmony. And so the story continues. Today there are heroes who

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:45.230
collect Pokemon and train hard in battle. Some of them even dream of becoming

00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:51.010
Pokemon masters. It is an exciting journey, but full of challenges too. Being a

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:56.500
trainer requires dedication and spirit. This road can certainly be long and

00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:00.000
difficult, but those who travel it will find many friends on

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.960
along the way.

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:05.910
Together, humans and Pokemon will carry on the story,

00:01:05.910 --> 00:01:08.930
facing new challenges and sharing new adventures

00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:11.730
that will become the tales of tomorrow.

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:15.660
But even tomorrow's stories may have started long ago,

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:19.190
like this tale that begins in the legendary past,

00:01:19.190 --> 00:01:21.730
before Pokeballs ever existed.

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:14.660
is with me.

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:31.150
Hear me, Ser Arran.

00:03:33.430 --> 00:03:50.820
What's the matter, Lucario?

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:56.030
The two armies are about to clash, Master, and our kingdom is caught between them.

00:03:56.390 --> 00:03:59.030
Once the fighting starts, we will all be destroyed.

00:04:02.270 --> 00:04:06.790
When the armies reach this palace, our kingdom will fall.

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:48.900
Do not flee the palace when the armies attack.

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:52.640
My fate will be the same as the rest of my kingdom.

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:58.960
- But your highness, there will be no survivors.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:06.520
your eyes don't worry about me master don't call me that I'm no longer your

00:06:06.520 --> 00:06:12.660
master I have abandoned the Queen and the kingdom I'll never return but that's

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:25.480
impossible master wait

00:06:36.170 --> 00:06:36.920
Master

00:07:00.090 --> 00:07:03.430
Coming from the tree of beginning, it's crying.

00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:17.770
And then the queen understood what Ser Arryn had done.

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:21.540
The wise knight, realizing that there was only one hope for the kingdom,

00:09:21.940 --> 00:09:25.630
had gone to the Tree of Beginning, the dwelling place of Mew.

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:27.190
Then what happened?

00:09:27.570 --> 00:09:30.000
The terrible forces that threatened her kingdom.

00:09:30.350 --> 00:09:32.240
were suddenly transformed.

00:09:32.240 --> 00:09:37.330
All at once, anger and hatred were changed into understanding and hope.

00:09:37.330 --> 00:09:42.840
Humans and Pokémon on both sides returned to their homes and peace was restored to the land.

00:09:42.840 --> 00:09:44.730
Really, Mom?

00:09:44.730 --> 00:09:46.190
Mm-hmm.

00:09:46.190 --> 00:09:52.000
And that is why Ser Arryn will forever be remembered as the true Guardian of Aura.

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:54.390
It's a great story!

00:09:54.390 --> 00:09:56.280
Can you read it again, please?

00:09:56.280 --> 00:09:57.630
Of course, dear.

00:09:57.630 --> 00:09:58.450
Hooray!

00:11:32.780 --> 00:11:39.220
As Ash continues his quest to become a Pokémon Master, he and his friends arrive at Cameran Palace.

00:11:39.220 --> 00:11:43.730
The Kingdom is holding a festival in honor of their legendary hero, Sir Aaron.

00:11:43.730 --> 00:11:46.870
And the main event will be a Pokémon competition.

00:11:46.870 --> 00:11:53.200
Trainers have come from near and far to compete, and the winner will be dubbed as this year's Guardian of the Aura.

00:11:53.200 --> 00:11:59.120
Well, I guess as part of the festival, everyone's dressing up in traditional costumes.

00:11:59.120 --> 00:12:00.000
What?

00:12:00.670 --> 00:12:06.670
any costumes it says here you can get him at the palace all right I'm gonna wear something

00:12:06.670 --> 00:12:14.530
heroic you should dress up Pikachu too Ash yeah that'd be pretty funny

00:12:47.340 --> 00:12:48.740
Pick just one!

00:12:48.740 --> 00:12:50.040
I need a cape!

00:12:51.640 --> 00:12:52.600
Let's see!

00:12:52.600 --> 00:12:58.680
Beega? Begachu?

00:13:01.280 --> 00:13:30.000
*Pikachu* Hey Pikachu! Like it? *laughs* Hey is that you? Tis I indeed! Wow Mei, you look great! Thank you brah! Now this is a big one!

00:13:30.670 --> 00:13:31.860
Right, Pikachu?

00:13:45.030 --> 00:13:46.190
Yeah, awesome!

00:13:46.190 --> 00:13:49.680
- Mika! - Well, guys, the competition will be starting soon.

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:51.880
Great! Pikachu, let's go!

00:13:51.880 --> 00:13:54.540
- Mika! -

00:14:00.090 --> 00:14:05.250
All right, so here's what I want to do show up at that shindig and pocket all of their Pokemon

00:14:06.430 --> 00:14:08.430
That's a brilliant idea, Jess

00:14:08.430 --> 00:14:10.430
You just let us know how that goes

00:14:12.430 --> 00:14:14.430
You two are coming as my dates

00:14:28.290 --> 00:14:30.000
Presenting her royal majesty

00:14:30.160 --> 00:14:35.160
the illustrious ruler of Cameron Palace, Lady Eileen!

00:14:35.160 --> 00:14:53.740
...and his noble deeds, we will begin our annual Pokémon contest!

00:14:53.740 --> 00:14:58.230
Oh-oh-oh-oh! I'm unbeatable!

00:17:11.230 --> 00:17:15.000
Pikachu wins! We have a new guardian for the year!

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:17.000
Catch 'em from Pallet Town!

00:17:33.610 --> 00:17:34.850
That was a great battle.

00:17:35.470 --> 00:17:36.610
Congratulations, you two.

00:17:36.690 --> 00:17:37.790
That guy's a girl.

00:17:38.660 --> 00:17:39.900
She was amazing.

00:17:40.520 --> 00:17:41.700
I can't believe it.

00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:42.680
Nice to meet you.

00:17:42.940 --> 00:17:43.740
I'm Kid.

00:17:43.980 --> 00:17:44.800
I'm Ash.

00:17:44.940 --> 00:17:47.240
And I'm Brock, at your service.

00:17:47.440 --> 00:17:51.080
I just wanted you to know that if you're ever in need of a squire, you can always count on me.

00:17:51.080 --> 00:17:52.000
Good grief.

00:17:52.150 --> 00:17:54.790
Each suit of armor isn't enough protection from here.

00:17:54.790 --> 00:17:55.470
Not here.

00:17:55.790 --> 00:17:56.090
Huh?

00:17:56.470 --> 00:17:56.850
Huh?

00:18:12.990 --> 00:18:22.660
This is the staff of the Guardian that once belonged to the great Sir Aaron.

00:18:22.660 --> 00:18:27.650
According to our tradition, the winner of the Pokemon contest is named the Aura Guardian

00:18:27.650 --> 00:18:30.000
for the year and is presented with this

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:39.570
on behalf of my kingdom ash it's yours thanks hmm this really belong to sir

00:18:39.570 --> 00:18:58.090
Aaron did you say something ma'am not a word now we'll begin the grand ball

00:18:58.090 --> 00:19:00.000
honoring sir Aaron and our new god

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:02.030
Please enjoy yourselves, everyone.

00:19:02.030 --> 00:19:25.020
Excuse me.

00:19:25.020 --> 00:19:27.020
May I have this dance, kid?

00:19:27.020 --> 00:19:29.030
You may.

00:19:29.030 --> 00:19:30.000
Why?

00:19:34.990 --> 00:19:38.430
There's no need to be nervous, Brock. Just put your arm around me.

00:19:38.430 --> 00:19:39.860
Oh, thank you!

00:19:56.640 --> 00:19:59.830
My Pokémon should come out and have fun at the party, too!

00:20:09.500 --> 00:20:27.420
me a moment guys don't not allowed to leave your chair as guardian you must

00:20:27.420 --> 00:20:30.000
sit still and look dignified all night

00:20:51.720 --> 00:20:54.220
Now's the perfect time to waltz off with some Pokémon!

00:20:54.220 --> 00:20:58.250
Oh, don't be a drag! I want to boogie the night away!

00:21:00.160 --> 00:21:00.660
Hi.

00:21:00.660 --> 00:21:02.400
You sure dance beautifully.

00:21:02.400 --> 00:21:04.080
Why, thank you.

00:21:04.080 --> 00:21:06.990
I'm dreaming. Please don't wake me!

00:21:06.990 --> 00:21:10.390
*cries*

00:21:10.390 --> 00:21:14.570
Have you ever seen this before?

00:21:14.570 --> 00:21:17.630
Oh, I get that sort of thing all the time.

00:21:17.630 --> 00:21:22.890
Personally, I always prefer dining to dancing.

00:21:22.890 --> 00:21:24.910
*gibberish*

00:21:24.910 --> 00:21:26.290
*gibberish*

00:21:26.290 --> 00:21:27.900
*gibberish*

00:21:27.900 --> 00:21:30.000
*gibberish*

00:21:30.120 --> 00:21:35.110
*Mumbling*

00:21:35.110 --> 00:21:41.080
We could really use a glass of punch.

00:21:41.080 --> 00:21:42.260
Coming right up!

00:21:42.260 --> 00:21:43.950
The lady wants punch!

00:21:48.840 --> 00:21:53.070
No.

00:22:01.050 --> 00:22:02.980
Are you there?

00:22:03.260 --> 00:22:04.800
Hi, kid. How's the party?

00:22:04.980 --> 00:22:07.340
It's fantastic. Too bad you couldn't be here.

00:22:07.520 --> 00:22:09.810
Who must have to keep this outfit running?

00:22:10.240 --> 00:22:13.040
For your information, I left the dance floor early.

00:22:13.450 --> 00:22:14.630
There's something I want to check out.

00:22:14.940 --> 00:22:16.940
I have a feeling it could really pay off.

00:22:17.040 --> 00:22:18.340
I certainly hope so.

00:22:18.520 --> 00:22:20.380
This operation is costing a fortune.

00:22:20.700 --> 00:22:22.040
We're seriously in the red.

00:22:22.200 --> 00:22:24.290
So you'd better come up with something pretty quick.

00:22:24.510 --> 00:22:27.430
Trust me, this trip will definitely be a success.

00:22:27.710 --> 00:22:30.000
And if it isn't, we can always go out and find real jobs.

00:22:30.990 --> 00:22:33.750
Thank you. I'm too old to work for a living.

00:22:33.990 --> 00:22:36.030
Don't sweat it, Banks. I've got a plan.

00:22:36.410 --> 00:22:38.270
Now there's a surprise.

00:22:39.050 --> 00:22:42.680
I'm going on a little excursion, and I need to see the layout of the palace.

00:22:43.110 --> 00:22:44.750
Will you transmit it to my data set?

00:22:45.110 --> 00:22:47.550
Hang on. I only have two minutes to go.

00:22:47.830 --> 00:22:48.690
Take a break.

00:22:48.890 --> 00:22:50.670
All right. One minute, then.

00:22:53.680 --> 00:22:57.060
Thanks for waiting. The data's streaming to you now.

00:22:57.280 --> 00:22:57.760
Wonderful.

00:22:58.420 --> 00:23:00.000
Would you mind telling me what this is...

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:04.480
There's a Mew hiding out here, and I'm planning on hunting it down.

00:23:04.480 --> 00:23:06.220
Ohh...

00:23:06.220 --> 00:23:12.880
Maybe Team Rocket ain't the only crooks in this here castle.

00:23:12.880 --> 00:23:13.880
Hmph.

00:23:13.880 --> 00:23:28.670
Wonder where Pikachu and the others ran off to.

00:23:28.670 --> 00:23:29.800
Huh?

00:23:31.920 --> 00:23:33.510
Munchlax.

00:23:33.510 --> 00:23:34.880
Munch.

00:23:34.880 --> 00:23:36.350
Munchlax?

00:23:36.350 --> 00:23:37.810
Mmm.

00:23:37.810 --> 00:23:41.810
Squirtle.

00:23:47.010 --> 00:23:48.110
How?

00:24:23.100 --> 00:24:25.080
Squirtle.

00:24:25.080 --> 00:24:28.630
Squirtle.

00:24:28.630 --> 00:24:29.280
Squirtle.

00:25:35.280 --> 00:25:37.080
So what's she up to?

00:25:39.320 --> 00:25:53.000
Munch, munch, munch, munch.

00:26:06.840 --> 00:26:15.180
Well, hello there, Mew.

00:26:15.180 --> 00:26:16.560
Reveal! Reveal!

00:26:16.560 --> 00:26:19.080
I want you to tag Mew with this transmitter.

00:26:19.080 --> 00:26:20.100
Oui!

00:26:20.100 --> 00:26:21.640
Reveal!

00:26:21.640 --> 00:26:23.050
Oui!

00:26:23.050 --> 00:26:26.660
Oui!

00:26:30.480 --> 00:26:34.700
Squirrel? What's going on?

00:26:34.700 --> 00:26:36.700
Meow!

00:26:36.700 --> 00:26:38.930
Hey, it's Meow!

00:26:38.930 --> 00:26:40.980
Meow!

00:26:40.980 --> 00:26:43.920
Meow!

00:26:43.920 --> 00:26:45.000
Meow!

00:26:46.280 --> 00:26:46.780
*munch munch*

00:27:19.360 --> 00:27:21.700
I told them to tag Mew, not tackle it.

00:27:27.550 --> 00:27:28.010
Ah!

00:27:28.010 --> 00:27:28.610
Ow!

00:27:32.810 --> 00:27:34.810
I got some sort of plan.

00:28:00.250 --> 00:28:12.990
I could do a ballet.

00:28:12.990 --> 00:28:16.260
What's you doing with two meows?

00:28:16.260 --> 00:28:18.250
Hmm? Um, you!

00:28:18.250 --> 00:28:25.350
Wee!

00:28:36.680 --> 00:28:39.380
Maybe it's time you laid off the Poké Block!

00:28:41.900 --> 00:28:56.160
I should send you both to Obedience School.

00:28:56.160 --> 00:28:57.240
Weeeeeee

00:28:57.240 --> 00:28:59.300
Nice!

00:28:59.300 --> 00:29:00.000
Much-much-much!

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:11.810
Lex!

00:29:11.810 --> 00:29:24.870
It's hard to believe this staff is hundreds of years old.

00:29:24.870 --> 00:29:26.980
And now I'm holding it.

00:29:31.400 --> 00:29:32.730
Sir Aaron!

00:29:32.730 --> 00:29:35.390
It's that voice again!

00:29:37.760 --> 00:29:41.040
We will now pay one last tribute to Sir Aaron.

00:29:41.040 --> 00:29:44.530
Our new guardian will give the signal to start the fireworks!

00:29:45.330 --> 00:29:47.390
Assume the pose of the guardian!

00:29:47.390 --> 00:29:48.950
What do you mean, "pose"?

00:29:48.950 --> 00:29:55.410
*crying*

00:30:43.240 --> 00:30:50.400
- Sir Aaron.

00:30:50.400 --> 00:30:51.890
- Telepathy.

00:30:51.890 --> 00:30:52.970
- Answer me.

00:30:52.970 --> 00:30:54.520
- I don't understand.

00:31:08.600 --> 00:31:09.850
- Who is that?

00:31:09.850 --> 00:31:10.990
- Lucario.

00:31:10.990 --> 00:31:12.550
- Lucario?

00:31:12.550 --> 00:31:13.750
- According to our legends,

00:31:13.750 --> 00:31:16.070
it's a Pokemon who served under Sir Aaron.

00:31:16.070 --> 00:31:17.640
- Right, from in here?

00:31:30.030 --> 00:31:33.420
I need answers.

00:31:33.420 --> 00:31:53.800
Hario, from now on this castle is going to be your new home and the place where you train.

00:31:53.800 --> 00:31:54.820
Yes.

00:31:54.820 --> 00:31:59.800
I'll teach you everything I have learned so that you can also learn how to be a user of Aura.

00:32:00.990 --> 00:32:09.030
Yes, the aura is inside, and soon one day you will learn to trust it.

00:32:43.210 --> 00:32:51.090
Lucario, I'm afraid I'm not who you think I am.

00:32:51.390 --> 00:32:57.890
You see, my name is Lady Eileen, and Lady Rin was one of my ancestors.

00:33:05.690 --> 00:33:08.800
You've been asleep for a long time, Lucario.

00:33:08.800 --> 00:33:10.310
Is it possible?

00:33:10.310 --> 00:33:12.190
I am telling you the truth.

00:33:12.190 --> 00:33:13.710
Uh...

00:33:13.710 --> 00:33:15.810
But...

00:33:15.810 --> 00:33:18.840
I was in this room just a few days ago.

00:33:18.840 --> 00:33:22.040
Please believe me, it may seem like days ago,

00:33:22.040 --> 00:33:25.960
but the reality is you haven't walked in this palace for centuries.

00:33:25.960 --> 00:33:28.770
Uh...

00:33:31.950 --> 00:33:37.440
According to the stories that were passed down, you vanished during the battle. Can you explain what happened?

00:33:38.020 --> 00:33:43.590
There were two huge armies on the move. Each side had sworn to destroy the other.

00:33:44.090 --> 00:33:48.930
The palace was trapped in the middle. I went out to see if there was a way to stop the fighting,

00:33:49.320 --> 00:33:55.600
but it was hopeless. So then how was Sir Aaron able to make peace? What? Our legend says Sir

00:33:55.600 --> 00:34:00.000
Aaron found a way to end the battle and save the palace. Impossible! Isn't that

00:34:01.090 --> 00:34:08.290
Sir Aaron deserted the Queen he fled and trapped me inside the staff in the legend. He's a hero

00:34:08.470 --> 00:34:10.210
Could it really be wrong?

00:34:10.210 --> 00:34:21.800
We'll look into it further and determine what is truth and what's fiction. I will do what I can to help you

00:34:22.600 --> 00:34:30.000
Lucario one thing hasn't changed. This palace is your home. Please feel free to stay here for as long as you like

00:34:32.240 --> 00:34:34.240
I am deeply grateful, your highness.

00:34:34.940 --> 00:34:37.480
Lucario, how come you thought I was Sir Aaron?

00:34:39.200 --> 00:34:42.400
Is it because this costume makes me look like him?

00:34:42.600 --> 00:34:46.210
No, the aura I sense in you is like Sir Aaron's.

00:34:46.690 --> 00:34:49.860
That Pokemon is really old, isn't it?

00:34:50.460 --> 00:34:54.040
It was locked inside of that staff for over a thousand years.

00:34:54.750 --> 00:34:55.190
Perfect!

00:34:55.350 --> 00:34:56.480
Of antiques!

00:34:56.830 --> 00:34:57.550
Hey, you guys!

00:34:59.040 --> 00:35:00.000
What is it?

00:35:02.240 --> 00:35:02.880
I saw Mew.

00:35:03.960 --> 00:35:05.900
Oh, what an adorable little boy.

00:35:06.240 --> 00:35:08.480
That costume he's wearing is so precious.

00:35:08.980 --> 00:35:10.760
He looks just like a little doll.

00:35:10.860 --> 00:35:12.060
You're not listening to me.

00:35:12.120 --> 00:35:13.680
We are, Max. Where's Mew?

00:35:13.820 --> 00:35:16.640
It just suddenly disappeared with Meowth and Pikachu.

00:35:17.960 --> 00:35:18.360
Mew.

00:35:19.810 --> 00:35:21.370
So, who are you?

00:35:21.570 --> 00:35:25.130
Oh, this is Lucario, a Pokemon who is sealed inside of the staff of the Guardian.

00:35:25.350 --> 00:35:27.050
Somehow he managed to set it free.

00:35:28.130 --> 00:35:30.000
Are you sure you saw Mew?

00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:31.940
and not a Pokemon who looked like it.

00:35:31.940 --> 00:35:32.820
Mew was here.

00:35:33.160 --> 00:35:36.340
I was on the roof when I saw Mew change into a pigeon.

00:35:36.810 --> 00:35:38.930
It flew away with Meowth and Pikachu.

00:35:39.540 --> 00:35:41.260
But why would Mew take them away?

00:35:41.420 --> 00:35:42.880
It was probably playing.

00:35:43.040 --> 00:35:45.500
Mew has a tradition of showing up here at the palace

00:35:45.500 --> 00:35:47.200
to play games and make mischief.

00:35:47.300 --> 00:35:49.360
It disappears with toys all the time

00:35:49.360 --> 00:35:51.080
and they're never to be seen again.

00:35:51.870 --> 00:35:53.810
Meowth, never to be seen again?

00:35:53.990 --> 00:35:56.830
We're the ones who are supposed to be doing all the Pokemon stealing.

00:35:57.170 --> 00:36:00.000
Did you miss the never to be seen again part?

00:36:00.030 --> 00:36:02.030
Does anybody know where Mew took them?

00:36:02.270 --> 00:36:03.870
I have to go rescue Pikachu.

00:36:11.730 --> 00:36:25.270
It appears there's a giant tree on top of that mountain.

00:36:25.630 --> 00:36:27.310
It's actually a rock formation.

00:36:27.840 --> 00:36:28.400
Amazing.

00:36:28.970 --> 00:36:30.000
Because of its great.

00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:33.000
our ancestors named it the tree of beginning.

00:36:33.000 --> 00:36:35.880
Oh, the tree of beginning, huh?

00:36:35.880 --> 00:36:37.740
That is where you will find Mew.

00:36:37.740 --> 00:36:39.690
Great!

00:36:39.690 --> 00:36:44.840
You must remember that Mew can change its form to look like any Pokémon in the world.

00:36:44.840 --> 00:36:48.840
It rarely shows its true form to humans, so you may have trouble recognizing it.

00:36:48.840 --> 00:36:51.760
Then how are we ever going to find where it went?

00:36:51.760 --> 00:36:54.760
The legend says Lucario could lead the Guardian to anyone,

